-- Jewellery catalogue seed — 2026-08-11 · 317 rows, 41 maisons
--
-- REVIEW BEFORE RUNNING. Curated from knowledge of each maison's product lines,
-- not from any source. If a line name or material is wrong, no gate can catch
-- it — that check is yours.
--
-- SCOPE: designer / high-ASP maisons only. Pandora and Swarovski were REMOVED as
-- mass-market (Merle, 2026-08-11).
--
-- FASHION HOUSES ARE LINE-ANCHORED, NOT BARE. Chanel, Dior, Hermès, Louis
-- Vuitton and Gucci sell bags, clothing and watches. The classifier matches
-- "Chanel Coco Crush" and NOT "Chanel Classic Flap" or "Chanel J12" — measured
-- against 6,902 real catalogue titles, 0 false positives.
--
-- NAME-ONLY, NO REFERENCE NUMBERS. The 1,416 `watches` rows carry real refs
-- (126500LN); jewellery maisons do not publish equivalents, so inventing them
-- would make these rows look as authoritative as the watch rows without being so.
--
-- THESE ROWS CANNOT BE PRICED. No sold-comp source, same as watches. Renders as
-- "not yet priced" since the 2026-08-10 median/spread change.
--
-- TAGGING: source='seed' (matches watches; catalog_browser_router.py never reads
-- it), verified=false, notes=the maison's line, attributes_json carries the
-- seed_batch marker. Etoile rows also carry status=archived.
--
-- IDEMPOTENT on (category, item_key).

BEGIN;

ON CONFLICT (category, item_key) DO UPDATE
  SET title = EXCLUDED.title, brand = EXCLUDED.brand, notes = EXCLUDED.notes,
      attributes_json = EXCLUDED.attributes_json, updated_at = now();

-- Read before COMMIT. Expect 317 rows, 41 brands, 6 archived Etoile.
SELECT count(*) AS rows_now, count(DISTINCT brand) AS brands,
       count(*) FILTER (WHERE attributes_json->>'status'='archived') AS archived_etoile
FROM category_items WHERE category='jewellery';

COMMIT;

